Subject: [PATCH] B5a: wire eo/dispatcher.py, eo/executor.py, eo/router.py to
 eo/capabilities.py
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Grounding note (repo-checked, same as B0's): none of the three files
imported eo.skill_library/eo.mcp_registry directly before this patch —
grep confirms zero hits. The real direct importers (agents/generic_worker.py,
eo/mcp_agent_tools.py) aren't in this patch's file list and don't match
eo/capabilities.py's wrapped signatures anyway. So this patch implements
the plan's parenthetical instead: '(or has no access at all and would
otherwise need it)' — each of the three files gets one real,
non-breaking eo/capabilities.py call site:

- eo/dispatcher.py: _is_known_capability() enriches the
  hallucinated_role_rejected event payload with a known_capability flag.
  Routing behavior (target_idx/reason) is unchanged.
- eo/executor.py: _available_capability_tags() adds a capability_tags
  field to every step's agent_start event payload, alongside the
  existing given_roles field. No dispatch branch or agent call shape
  changes — agents/generic_worker.py itself is untouched.
- eo/router.py: new capability_registration_gaps(), parallel to
  validate_registry_coverage() but non-raising (capability-layer
  coverage is explicitly a starting set, not a hard invariant, per B1's
  own CAPABILITY_SEED docstring).

All three lookups are wrapped in try/except — a broken/unavailable
capability store degrades to a safe default rather than breaking
dispatch or routing.

Acceptance: grep confirms no eo.skill_library/eo.mcp_registry imports
in dispatcher.py/executor.py/router.py (still zero, as before this
patch); all three now import eo.capabilities.list_capabilities and use
it.

Tests: extended test_eo_dispatcher.py, test_eo_executor.py, and
test_eo_router.py with cases that mock eo.capabilities.list_capabilities
and assert the call is actually made and its result reaches the
relevant payload/return value, plus a defensive test per file for
lookup-failure behavior.

DEFERRED.md: added a 'Deferred during Patch B5a' section (on top of
the already-merged B2 redaction-coverage entry) — per-role capability
granularity, and generic_worker.run() not yet receiving capability
context.
